WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.100
From March 2027, apple must open australian iPhones to rival app stores. This is MAG 7 Daily,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:12.660
episode 30. After that court order, meta's quarter, and a new share class, then a bigger

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.280
foldable order, then one assistant on two car screens. Australia's federal court set

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.920
the start at noon in Melbourne on March 1st, 2027, for users whose apple account region

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:30.320
is Australia. The order follows in August 2025 finding that Apple misused its market power over

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.540
distribution and payments. Developer program members worldwide can join. Apple cannot charge

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:41.900
for access to rival stores or direct downloads, and it has to hand over tools on substantially

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.420
the same terms as its own store. It cannot force its payment system, transaction reports,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.520
or an audit of other payments. On App Store apps, fees for those other payments are

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.840
capped at the physical goods rate plus genuine extra cost.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.680
Outside apps still need a security or privacy scan and notarization by Apple or a qualified

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.460
third party.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.040
Epic Games told Reuters that Fortnite comes back to Australia's app store today, and

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.660
that order does not wait for March.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.420
Australia was the only country left out when Fortnite returned worldwide in May.

00:01:15.494 --> 00:01:17.674
Meta's quarter is the capital spending print.

00:01:18.254 --> 00:01:21.294
Yesterday the open question was whether that spending would move.

00:01:21.294 --> 00:01:31.414
Today met a narrowed 2026 capital expenditure to $135 to $145 billion from $130 to $145 billion.

00:01:31.974 --> 00:01:40.314
Revenue was $64.60 billion, up 26%. Family daily active people averaged $3.64 billion

00:01:40.314 --> 00:01:48.034
in September, up 3%. Add Impressions rose 10%, and the average price per ad rose 14%.

00:01:48.034 --> 00:01:55.374
Costs were 51.61 billion dollars, up 68 percent, including a $9.89 billion charge.

00:01:55.814 --> 00:02:00.654
That charge sits on an August deal with 52 attorneys general over teen mental health

00:02:00.654 --> 00:02:05.054
and social media, with payments of up to about $18.59 billion.

00:02:05.974 --> 00:02:12.694
Strip the charge out and operating income would have been $22.88 billion, not $12.99 billion,

00:02:12.694 --> 00:02:17.214
and diluted earnings $7.40, not $3.83.

00:02:17.854 --> 00:02:23.674
The quarter's capital spending, including finance lease principle, was $34.91 billion.

00:02:24.674 --> 00:02:28.854
Fullyer expenses are now $175-179 billion.

00:02:29.814 --> 00:02:35.574
Reality labs losses are guided to $18-19 billion, lower than 2025.

00:02:35.574 --> 00:02:41.774
4th quarter revenue is guided to 73-76 billion dollars with foreign exchange

00:02:41.774 --> 00:02:48.274
about a 1% headwind and the 4th quarter tax rate to 15-17%. Cash and

00:02:48.274 --> 00:02:54.534
marketable securities were 82.45 billion dollars. Operating cash flow was 32.79

00:02:54.534 --> 00:03:03.254
billion. Free cash flow was negative 2.12 billion. Headcount was 66,775, down 15

00:03:04.034 --> 00:03:10.914
FX leaders also reports a $25 billion new Mexico penalty over misleading data privacy practices.

00:03:11.514 --> 00:03:16.834
Bloomberg reports a new non-voting share class that could help pay for acquisitions and other costs.

00:03:17.514 --> 00:03:22.674
The information reports the overhaul was shaped by expectations of raising hundreds of billions of dollars,

00:03:23.094 --> 00:03:25.254
and by a proposed California wealth tax.

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:31.034
Mark Zuckerberg said the quarter hit major milestones toward personal superintelligence for everyone,

00:03:31.034 --> 00:03:37.466
including Muse and Muse Wonder, which he called the first frontier model, Apple's foldable

00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:43.106
order book moved. Digitime says Foxconn and component makers were told to raise iPhone

00:03:43.106 --> 00:03:51.326
Duo output by about 44% from 9.7 million units to 14 million across a full 12 months, not

00:03:51.326 --> 00:03:57.086
just the rest of 2026. Apple last week called pre-order demand nothing short of extraordinary.

00:03:57.086 --> 00:04:05.506
In 30 minutes of pre-orders opening on October 16th, United States shipping estimates hit January 25th on every configuration.

00:04:06.086 --> 00:04:12.666
Digitime says the higher target still depends on assembly after earlier trouble with assembly, displays, and hinges.

00:04:13.126 --> 00:04:24.086
It forecasts global foldable shipments up 25.7% in 2026 and 59.1% in 2027 against 7.4% in 2025.

00:04:24.086 --> 00:04:30.726
The phone launches October 23rd, starting at $1,999 in the United States.

00:04:31.655 --> 00:04:37.115
Cognizant, in an Education Times report, has put 18,000 engineers on Google's Gemini,

00:04:37.675 --> 00:04:39.055
framed as tools for businesses.

00:04:39.675 --> 00:04:45.555
Megazone Cloud, Chosun Bizz reports, has a resale nod for Amazon's Gov Cloud, and is pointing

00:04:45.555 --> 00:04:48.335
it at United States public sector and defense buyers.

00:04:48.335 --> 00:04:54.555
A century and a half of Kia's chemistry data is coming into Microsoft co-pilot, R&amp;D World

00:04:54.555 --> 00:04:57.955
Reports, as a research reference set inside that assistant.

00:04:58.695 --> 00:05:03.935
NVIDIA has widened Cosmos with training tools, simulation checkpoints, and data factory

00:05:03.935 --> 00:05:06.675
blueprints for world models used in physical AI.

00:05:07.275 --> 00:05:11.295
It says the platform sits in the top five on six open model leaderboards.

00:05:11.735 --> 00:05:16.295
What cuts against the Australian opening is that Apple still notarizes outside apps,

00:05:16.295 --> 00:05:22.155
or requires a qualified third party to do it, and can still pull an outside app for harmful content,

00:05:22.675 --> 00:05:28.015
a real security risk, or the law. Apple told Reuters it will appeal and ask for a pause

00:05:28.015 --> 00:05:34.455
on intellectual property and store security. Between February 1st and February 15th, it can apply,

00:05:34.855 --> 00:05:41.906
with evidence to push enforcement to May 3rd, 2027. Google and Apple now share a voice on the dashboard.

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:46.146
In 2019, Maps Traffic Reports lived only on phones.

00:05:46.706 --> 00:05:49.566
Early 2024, Hazard Pins reached CarPlay.

00:05:50.126 --> 00:05:52.146
Later that year, they reached Android Auto.

00:05:52.726 --> 00:05:55.586
Today, Google put Gemini inside Maps on CarPlay.

00:05:56.106 --> 00:06:00.686
The Mac observer calls that the first built-in voice for this navigation app on that screen.

00:06:01.386 --> 00:06:02.706
The United States has it now.

00:06:03.266 --> 00:06:04.646
A wider release is underway.

00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:08.486
On an active route, an icon on the right edge opens Gemini.

00:06:08.486 --> 00:06:14.106
You can ask for a park with city views, a time that is not crowded and stays fair, then

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.466
a route that skips tolls.

00:06:15.946 --> 00:06:17.746
The same voice can report a disruption.

00:06:18.366 --> 00:06:22.946
That screen now matches Android Auto and the voice tools added to the iPhone Maps app

00:06:22.946 --> 00:06:23.586
last year.

00:06:24.186 --> 00:06:26.546
Before today, those tools stayed on the handset.

00:06:27.066 --> 00:06:31.706
Bogdan Popa at Auto Evolution already has it on an iPhone 15 Pro in Europe.

00:06:32.306 --> 00:06:33.766
A follow-up keeps its subject.

00:06:33.766 --> 00:06:38.626
best cappuccino nearby, then whether it is expensive, then navigate there.

00:06:39.146 --> 00:06:44.846
He found CarPlay more refined than Android Auto, where Gemini has been buggy since late 2025.

00:06:45.686 --> 00:06:49.986
Last month Google retired assistant on Android Auto, so there is no switchback.

00:06:50.586 --> 00:06:55.726
Drivers had called it to chatty, and some said it could not call 911 or place a phone call.

00:06:56.426 --> 00:07:00.346
On CarPlay, ordinary speech can file heavy traffic without a set phrase.

00:07:00.346 --> 00:07:07.246
Apple owns the glass, Google owns maps, Gemini, and Ways. Ways still takes objects in the road,

00:07:07.646 --> 00:07:13.206
broken lights, floods, and potholes. Maps stays with accidents, road works, and speed cameras,

00:07:13.626 --> 00:07:19.406
and now also pulls police reports from Ways. For Apple, a Google app gains a conversational layer

00:07:19.406 --> 00:07:24.646
the day before the duo goes on sale, and Apple is not shipping the model. For Google,

00:07:24.646 --> 00:07:27.706
CarPlay is no longer the screen where that voice was missing.

00:07:28.831 --> 00:07:34.091
Jensen Huang told the UK NeoCloud end-scale to work around the clock after early setbacks

00:07:34.091 --> 00:07:35.771
getting some data centers online.

